{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 103, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-output shortcut where none existed gives a much larger gain than replacing a conv on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the residual shortcut is far more damaging than deleting a conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without the 0->3 shortcut, an extra path into the output node is more valuable."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When node 2 lacks a direct input, a conv reading from it contributes little."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Cutting node 1's input hurts more when node 1 feeds the output through a conv."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv with pooling loses capacity, whereas replacing a skip barely does."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Swapping out a harmful pooling op gains more than adding a new path."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Downgrading conv3x3 to conv1x1 hurts, while upgrading skip to conv1x1 helps."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "A second shortcut is redundant when 0->3 is already skip, so losing the conv on edge 5 costs more."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "If node 1 is dead because e